Hello David,

Daniel Chung is a resident at 6-585 Corydon ave. I have included him in
this email.

He has been a resident here since 2021 and he was not provided with the
storage unit despite a unit existing that was clearly marked #6 correlated
with his suite. Storage was not included in his lease agreement but the
Landlord has attempted to persuade me that the unit I have has been
provided as a 'courtesy' to me which has been subsequently recognized as a
service provided as they have since given me notice that they are
withdrawing the service of storage unit and I will be receiving a rent
decrease based on this, This should be extended to Mr, Chung as she was
denied the service on the basis of avoiding following RTB protocol that
would have resulted in necessitating rent decrease.

In addition, Mr. Chung has also been offered laundry service renovation
which he has refused. On May 1 laundry services will be withdrawn and this
will necessitate a reduction in his rent as well.

Please note that my charge is that Thorwin Properties has practiced
deception and fraud in denying Mr. Chung access to the storage locker in
order to deceitfully avoid following RTB procedure which should result in
rent decrease.

The landlord has engaged in lies and exploitation of both tenant and RTB
and this must be addressed as soon as possible.

You may choose to include me in email responses as Mr. Chung speaks English
as an additional language and I am offering to facilitate communication.

You can reach Daniel Hung at =E2=80=AD+1 (204) 952-3037=E2=80=AC.

All the best,
Evan Rosner


